Tell an embedder which stack the current Determinate Nix fiber runs on.

A Python primop that an evaluator thread calls runs on a fiber's stack.
CPython 3.14 measures its stack margin against the thread's own stack,
so in `_Py_Dealloc` the fiber's stack reads as past the limit and every
GC-tracked object goes to the thread's `delete_later` list. That list
drains only on a later free with room to spare, which never comes, and
the thread state goes away with it full: none of 100 objects freed
(test_a_primop_on_an_evaluator_thread_frees_what_it_drops,
nixidae/nixidae#1083). Calls are unaffected, because their check also
wants the stack pointer near the limit.

`PyUnstable_ThreadState_SetStackProtection` takes the right bounds, and
only Determinate Nix knows them: the fiber keeps the stack it started
on, and `currentFiberStack()` returns it.

Applies after nix-determinate-interrupted-thunk-recovers.
