+/**
+ * The stack the current fiber was started on, guard page included, or
+ * an empty span outside a fiber. An embedded runtime that compares its
+ * stack pointer against the thread's own stack, such as CPython 3.14,
+ * needs these bounds to run on a fiber. Code inside a coroutine body
+ * runs on another stack, so a caller checks that its stack pointer is
+ * inside.
+ */
+std::span<std::byte> currentFiberStack();
